    <description>&lt;b&gt;Status (as of Oct 14, 2026):&lt;/b&gt; Open – ribbon cutting July 19, 2026 (Oshtemo Twp). Not cleared of snow in winter.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Facility:&lt;/b&gt; Shared-use trail, ~2 mi, 10-ft crushed limestone (not paved)&lt;br&gt;Former Fruit Belt rail corridor. Trailheads with paved parking at Flesher Field and 6th Street. Line geometry from the KATS October 2026 facilities layer.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sources:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.oshtemo.org/Departments/Parks-Recreation-Department/Fruit-Belt-Rail-Trail-Development"&gt;Oshtemo Twp – Fruit Belt Rail Trail Development&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.oshtemo.org/Departments/Media-Communications/Newsletter/Summer-2026-Newsletter"&gt;Oshtemo Twp – Summer 2026 Newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://services8.arcgis.com/iMB25Rg6ZW5ZL5YH/arcgis/rest/services/Existing_Facilities_October_2026/FeatureServer/0"&gt;KATS Existing Facilities October 2026 (ArcGIS layer, edited Oct 7, 2026)&lt;/a&gt;</description>
    <styleUrl>#upd2026-sup</styleUrl>
