   <Placemark>
    <name>Ada pedestrian bridge over the Thornapple River (new 2026)</name>
    <description>&lt;b&gt;Status (as of Oct 15, 2026):&lt;/b&gt; Open – expected to open July 16, 2026.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Facility:&lt;/b&gt; 270-ft pedestrian/bike bridge&lt;br&gt;Links Legacy Park and downtown Ada to the township trail network to the south. Location approximate.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sources:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.fox17online.com/news/local-news/east-grand-rapids-forest-hills-cascade/as-ada-pedestrian-bridge-nears-opening-businesses-look-ahead-to-increased-foot-traffic"&gt;FOX17 – As Ada pedestrian bridge nears opening (June 2026)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://grandriver.network/2026/04/spring-construction/"&gt;Grand River Greenway – 2026 construction season (Apr 2026)&lt;/a&gt;</description>
    <styleUrl>#upd2026-suppt</styleUrl>
    <Point>
     <coordinates>-85.489,42.9545,0</coordinates>
    </Point>
   </Placemark>
   <Placemark>
    <name>Wyoming 28th St pedestrian bridge (new 2025)</name>
    <description>&lt;b&gt;Status (as of Oct 15, 2026):&lt;/b&gt; Open – opened September 2025.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Facility:&lt;/b&gt; 12-ft pedestrian/bike bridge over 28th St&lt;br&gt;Connects Wyoming City Center and Wyoming High School (south) with Pinery Park and the trail network (north).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sources:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.wyomingmi.gov/CityCenter/PedestrianBridge"&gt;City of Wyoming – Pedestrian Bridge&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://services5.arcgis.com/X42k956XlfnIoN3d/arcgis/rest/services/OffStSharedUseFY26_29TIP/FeatureServer/0"&gt;GVMC non-motorized project list (route lines)&lt;/a&gt;</description>
    <styleUrl>#upd2026-suppt</styleUrl>
    <Point>
     <coordinates>-85.69944,42.91341,0</coordinates>
    </Point>
   </Placemark>
   <Placemark>
    <name>Idema Explorers Trail – Bayou segment (new 2025)</name>
    <description>&lt;b&gt;Status (as of Oct 15, 2026):&lt;/b&gt; Open – completed June 2025, finishing the 24-mi Grand Crossings Loop.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Facility:&lt;/b&gt; Shared-use trail incl. a 14-ft bridge over Stearns Bayou&lt;br&gt;Robinson Twp. Alignment from Ottawa County's future-trail data (not yet in its existing-trail data).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sources:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://grandrivergreenway.org/2025/06/20/bayou-segment/"&gt;Grand River Greenway – Bayou Segment of Idema Explorers Trail completed (June 2025)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://gis.miottawa.org/arcgis/rest/services/HostedServices/NonMotorizedPathways/FeatureServer"&gt;Ottawa County non-motorized pathways (updated May 2025)&lt;/a&gt;</description>
