   <Placemark>
    <name>Portage St (Cork-Stockbridge) Bike Lane (new 2026)</name>
    <description>&lt;b&gt;Status (as of Oct 14, 2026):&lt;/b&gt; Built Aug 3 – Sept 30, 2026 (final markings week of Sept 28). Now listed as an existing bike lane in KATS's facilities layer (updated Oct 7, 2026).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Facility:&lt;/b&gt; Bike lanes both sides (4-to-3 lane road diet with center turn lane)&lt;br&gt;Also adds median refuge islands and rapid flashing beacons at Cambridge, Roseland, Franklin, Lay Blvd, Hays Park, Clinton and Egleston. Connects to the existing Portage St bike lanes north of Stockbridge.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sources:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.kalamazoocity.org/Community/Projects/2026/Portage-Street-Lane-Conversion"&gt;City of Kalamazoo – Portage Street Lane Conversion (2026)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://wwmt.com/news/local/kalamazoo-commissioners-approve-portage-street-road-diet-project-6-1-vote-turn-lane-safety-bike-pedestrian-children-school-speeding-local-west-michigan-wwmt"&gt;WWMT – Commissioners approve Portage Street road diet (May 11, 2026)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://services8.arcgis.com/iMB25Rg6ZW5ZL5YH/arcgis/rest/services/Existing_Facilities_October_2026/FeatureServer/0"&gt;KATS Existing Facilities October 2026 (ArcGIS layer, edited Oct 7, 2026)&lt;/a&gt;</description>
