   <Placemark>
    <name>Ann St separated bike lanes, Turner Ave to Plainfield Ave (new 2025)</name>
    <description>&lt;b&gt;Status (as of Oct 15, 2026):&lt;/b&gt; Built 2025 (raised, separated lanes east of the river; buffered lanes to the west).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Facility:&lt;/b&gt; Separated bike lanes&lt;br&gt;Local reports note gaps of about 1.3 mi total, mostly on the river bridge and at the Turner Ave / I-196 intersections.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sources:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.fox17online.com/news/local-news/grand-rapids/bins-in-the-bike-lane-where-to-put-trash-recycling-on-newly-repaved-ann-street"&gt;FOX17 – Bins in the bike lane on newly repaved Ann Street (Dec 2025)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://urbangr.org/MobilityUpdate202510"&gt;UrbanGR – Mobility Update, Oct 2025&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.grandrapidsmi.gov/departments/engineering/road-construction/recent-construction-projects/ann-street-nw-monroe-ave-nw-to-turner-ave-nw/"&gt;City of Grand Rapids – Ann St NW (Monroe to Turner)&lt;/a&gt;</description>
