  <Folder>
   <name>Construction Zone: Kalamazoo Ave (2026-2028)</name>
   <Placemark>
    <name>CAUTION: Kalamazoo Ave reconstruction zone (Jul 2026 – 2028)</name>
    <description>&lt;b&gt;Status (as of Oct 14, 2026):&lt;/b&gt; Under construction since July 13, 2026. Westnedge–Harrison through 2027; Stuart neighborhood section 2028.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Facility:&lt;/b&gt; Work zone – not a bike facility&lt;br&gt;Full rebuild ahead of two-way conversion; one lane usually open, with closures and detours. The city's plan pages for Kalamazoo Ave do not show bike lanes. The KRVT's downtown section has been detoured onto the Michigan Ave two-way cycle track (posted May 2024 – summer 2026; check signs). Other Streets for All downtown work: W Main late 2026/2027, Douglas 2027, Michigan Ave 2028–29 (parts get separated bike lanes), South &amp;amp; Lovell 2030.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sources:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.kalamazoocity.org/Community/Projects/Streets-for-All/Streets-for-All-Kalamazoo-Ave-2026-2028"&gt;City of Kalamazoo – Streets for All: Kalamazoo Ave (2026–2028)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.kalamazoocity.org/Community/Projects/Streets-for-All/SFA-Frequently-Asked-Questions"&gt;City of Kalamazoo – Streets for All FAQ&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.kzooparks.org/Parks-Facilities/Kalamazoo-River-Valley-Trail"&gt;Kzoo Parks – Kalamazoo River Valley Trail&lt;/a&gt;</description>
    <styleUrl>#upd2026-zone</styleUrl>
